radeonsi/vce: validate the feedback size before reporting it.

rvce_get_feedback() reports ptr[4] - ptr[9] (the firmware's end and start
offsets in the bitstream buffer) without any check. After a failed or hung
VCE job these words are garbage: the difference can wrap or exceed the
buffer, and the VA frontend hands it on as the coded segment size, so the
application is told to copy past the end of its coded buffer (Chromium
150: "Insufficient output buffer size: 2097152, the buffer segment size:
2386084", Radeon Pro 560 / Polaris 11, VCE 3.4, under OpenIndiana). The
function also dereferences the feedback buffer when rvce_encode_bitstream()
could not create it, and when the map fails.

Remember the size the firmware was allowed to write
(allowedMaxBitstreamSize = bs_size - bs_offset) with the feedback buffer,
report 0 bytes and PIPE_VIDEO_FEEDBACK_METADATA_ENCODE_FLAG_FAILED for a
missing or unmappable feedback buffer or an impossible size, so vaMapBuffer
returns VA_STATUS_ERROR_ENCODING_ERROR instead of a bogus segment. This is
robustness only: it does not prevent whatever made the firmware fail.

Upstream code (unchanged on main, 2026-11-20):
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/main/src/gallium/drivers/radeonsi/mm/radeon_vce.c
Upstreamable (not yet submitted).

